<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18100" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀφαίρ-εσις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εως</span>,
			ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>taking away, carrying off, removal,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Cri.</u>
				46c
			</span></i> (pl.); <i>putting off,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ θνητοῦ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hierocl.
					<u>in CA</u>
					27p.483M.
				</span></i>
			; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσθεσις,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Lyc.</u>
				13
			</span></i> (pl.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> as
			law-term, <i>assertion of freedom of a reputed slave,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hyp.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				23
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>amputation,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Archig.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				47.13.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in Logic,
				<i>abstraction,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ, δι᾽ ἀφαιρέσεως,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Cael.</u>
				299a16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>EN</u>
				1142a18
			</span></i>; esp. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἐξ ἀ.</span>”
				<i>mathe-matics,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>AP</u>
					0.81b3
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				1061a29
			</span></i>, al.; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ προσθέσεως,</span>
			ib. <i><span class="en">
				1077b9
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἐν ἀ. ὄντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>de An.</u>
					429b18
				</span></i>
			, al.:—Cicero jokes on this term, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Att.</u>
				6.1.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> Gramm.,
				<i>removal</i> of initial letters, as in <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σῦς ὗς,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Choerob.
				<u>in Theod.</u>
				1p.148H.
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				A.D.
				<u>Pron.</u>
				55.13
			</span></i>, al.; also of medial letters, ib.<i><span class="en">
				93.13
			</span></i>; of feet in verse, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόσθεσις,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				220 iii 3
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
